# text = The Maypole -- by which term from henceforth is meant the house , and not its sign -- the Maypole was an old building , with more gable ends than a lazy man would care to count on a sunny day ; huge zig-zag chimneys , out of which it seemed as though even smoke could not choose but come in more than naturally fantastic shapes , imparted to it in its tortuous progress ; and vast stables , gloomy , ruinous , and empty .
