# text = The evening with which we have to do , was neither a summer nor an autumn one , but the twilight of a day in March , when the wind howled dismally among the bare branches of the trees , and rumbling in the wide chimneys and driving the rain against the windows of the Maypole Inn , gave such of its frequenters as chanced to be there at the moment an undeniable reason for prolonging their stay , and caused the landlord to prophesy that the night would certainly clear at eleven o'clock precisely ,-- which by a remarkable coincidence was the hour at which he always closed his house .
