# text = If he had spoken boldly , persisted in questioning her , detained her when she rose to leave the room , made any kind of protest , instead of silently compromising himself , as he felt he had done , he would have been more at ease said Gabriel , putting his wig on one side to scratch his head with greater ease , and looking ruefully at the fire He took his wig off outright as he made this reflection , and , warming his handkerchief at the fire began to rub and polish his bald head with it , until it glistened again said the locksmith , softening under this soothing process , and stopping to smile and here was the vexation he cried , looking in and nodding said the locksmith cried Barnaby , glancing over his shoulder asked Gabriel returned the locksmith he replied , shaking his head the idiot whispered in his ear , and then fell back with a look of triumph said the locksmith , with a grave look he replied , keeping away from him As he spoke , he caught up the light , and waved it with a wild laugh above his head said the locksmith , exerting all his influence to keep him calm and quiet he rejoined , with widely-opened eyes said the locksmith he echoed softly , drawing closer to him replied the locksmith said Barnaby , passing his arm through Varden's , and peering close into his face as he answered in a whisper said Varden , imagining that he traced some connection between this vision and what had actually occurred .
# sent_id = 283
