# text = It was on one of those mornings , common in early spring , when the year , fickle and changeable in its youth like all other created things , is undecided whether to step backward into winter or forward into summer , and in its uncertainty inclines now to the one and now to the other , and now to both at once -- wooing summer in the sunshine , and lingering still with winter in the shade -- it was , in short , on one of those mornings , when it is hot and cold , wet and dry , bright and lowering , sad and cheerful , withering and genial , in the compass of one short hour , that old John Willet , who was dropping asleep over the copper boiler , was roused by the sound of a horse's feet , and glancing out at window , beheld a traveller of goodly promise , checking his bridle at the Maypole door .
