# text = The guest who received him , on the other hand , seemed to feel that the contrast between them was all in his favour , and to derive a quiet exultation from it which put him more at his ease than ever said this gentleman , without the least appearance of embarrassment or reserve returned the other , waving his hand returned the other , leaning his arm upon the chimney-piece , and turning a haughty look upon the occupant of the easy-chair said Mr Chester , tapping his snuff-box , and following with a smile the impatient gesture he had made -- perhaps unconsciously -- towards his sword returned the other returned the other , most composedly cried Mr Haredale , drawing his breath returned the other , tasting his wine with great deliberation said Mr Haredale rejoined the other , interrupting him with the same complacency returned the other said Mr Chester returned Mr Haredale impatiently said the other , crossing his legs , and smiling as he held his glass up in the bright glow of the fire he returned , sipping his wine said Mr Haredale , after a short silence cried Mr Chester , lazily filling his glass again , and pulling out his toothpick retorted Mr Haredale fiercely said the other , not at all disturbed said Mr Haredale , striding to the table , and laying his hand upon it heavily returned the other , rocking himself to and fro as in assent , and nodding at the fire said Mr Haredale , who had been pacing to and fro rejoined Mr Chester with the utmost blandness said Mr Haredale returned the other , with his most affable smile said Mr Haredale , with an expression of impatience he was at no pains to conceal he added in a lower tone said Mr Chester , restoring some errant faggots to their places in the grate with the toe of his boot said Mr Haredale , drawing on his glove returned the other , sipping his wine he added , helping himself again said Mr Haredale , after a short silence , during which he had eyed his smiling face from time to time intently said the other , with a nod pursued Mr Haredale returned the other , shrugging his shoulders and stretching himself more comfortably before the fire said Mr Haredale returned the other , relishing a pinch of snuff extremely said Mr Haredale , moving to and fro , and stopping , and moving on again , like one who was ill at ease said Mr Chester , rising with a graceful indolence returned the other drily , ' I know the way .
