# text = Joe set spurs to the grey mare , and was at his side directly he said , touching his hat The gentleman smiled and nodded said Joe said Edward , good-humouredly sighed Joe said Joe after a short silence returned Edward Joe shook his head ; but there was something so cheery in the buoyant hopeful manner of this speech , that his spirits rose under its influence , and communicated as it would seem some new impulse even to the grey mare , who , breaking from her sober amble into a gentle trot , emulated the pace of Edward Chester's horse , and appeared to flatter herself that he was doing his very best .
