# text = The young man leant his head upon his hand , and made no answer said the father rising , and walking slowly to and fro -- stopping now and then to glance at himself in the mirror , or survey a picture through his glass , with the air of a connoisseur returned the son , raising his head for a moment , and then falling into his former attitude said the father returned his father more compassionately than ever muttered Edward returned his father With these words , the father , who had been arranging his cravat in the glass , while he uttered them in a disconnected careless manner , withdrew , humming a tune as he went .
