# text = To be shelterless and alone in the open country , hearing the wind moan and watching for day through the whole long weary night ; to listen to the falling rain , and crouch for warmth beneath the lee of some old barn or rick , or in the hollow of a tree ; are dismal things -- but not so dismal as the wandering up and down where shelter is , and beds and sleepers are by thousands ; a houseless rejected creature .
