# text = I know faltered Dolly Dolly hesitated for a little while , and somewhat emboldened by his manner , said at last Dolly hesitated again , and not being able to decide upon any other course of action , burst into tears said Mr Haredale Dolly had what is popularly called a spirit of her own , and being now fairly at bay , made the best of it she rejoined , trembling and frightened as she was said Mr Haredale Not feeling quite certain , as she afterwards said , whether he might not be ' coming over her ' with these compliments , Dolly kept as far from him as she could , cried again , and resolved to defend her pocket ( for the letter was there ) to the last extremity said Mr Haredale after a short silence , during which a smile , as he regarded her , had struggled through the gloom and melancholy that was natural to his face answered Dolly , not sure but he was bantering her said Mr Haredale replied Dolly said Mr Haredale Dolly didn't let him , nor did she wait for him to try , for the words had no sooner passed his lips than she was out of the room , out of the house , and in the fields again .
