# text = He became thoughtful again , and the toothpick was in requisition he continued Men who are thoroughly false and hollow , seldom try to hide those vices from themselves ; and yet in the very act of avowing them , they lay claim to the virtues they feign most to despise say they The more they affect to deny the existence of any sincerity in the world , the more they would be thought to possess it in its boldest shape ; and this is an unconscious compliment to Truth on the part of these philosophers , which will turn the laugh against them to the Day of Judgment .
