# text = The master , who had only heard his foot upon the ground and had not taken the trouble to turn round and look at him , shut his book , and pursued the train of ideas his entrance had disturbed he said , handling his snuff-box replied Hugh , striding in , followed by a dog , as rough and sullen as himself returned the other , raising his head a little from the cushion and carelessly surveying him from top to toe said Hugh impatiently said Hugh returned Mr Chester rising , slowly pulling off the loose robe he wore , and sitting down before the dressing-glass Having said this in the politest and blandest tone possible , he went on dressing , and took no further notice of his guest , who stood in the same spot as uncertain what to do next , eyeing him sulkily from time to time he said , after a long silence returned Mr Chester
