# text = This was said with a smile which implied -- or Hugh thought it did He answered that he would said his patron , with an air of the very kindest patronage Hugh accepted it from his hand , and looking stealthily at his smiling face , drank the contents in silence said Mr Chester , in his most winning manner was the sullen answer , with something approaching to a bow said Hugh , quickly exclaimed his patron , with a condescending smile said Hugh , abruptly rejoined his patron , looking at him through his glass said Hugh said Mr Chester Hugh made no rejoinder , but whistling to his dog , who sprung up at the sound and came jumping and sporting about him , bade his sympathising friend good night Hugh truckled before the hidden meaning of these words as much as such a being could , and crept out of the door so submissively and subserviently -- with an air , in short , so different from that with which he had entered -- that his patron on being left alone , smiled more than ever he said , as he took a pinch of snuff
