# text = His older childhood , too ; the strange imaginings he had ; his terror of certain senseless things -- familiar objects he endowed with life ; the slow and gradual breaking out of that one horror , in which , before his birth , his darkened intellect began ; how , in the midst of all , she had found some hope and comfort in his being unlike another child , and had gone on almost believing in the slow development of his mind until he grew a man , and then his childhood was complete and lasting ; one after another , all these old thoughts sprung up within her , strong after their long slumber and bitterer than ever .
