# text = That was all SHE knew said Mr Haredale , presenting himself before this new tenant he returned retorted the other in a suppressed tone and voice said Mr Chester returned Mr Haredale said the locksmith bluntly said Mr Chester he said , turning languidly to Mr Haredale Mr Haredale glanced at him -- not fondly or admiringly -- smiled , and held his peace said Mr Chester said Mr Haredale returned his smiling friend echoed Mr Haredale Mr Haredale stood in the widow's parlour with the door-key in his hand , gazing by turns at Mr Chester and at Gabriel Varden , and occasionally glancing downward at the key as in the hope that of its own accord it would unlock the mystery ; until Mr Chester , putting on his hat and gloves , and sweetly inquiring whether they were walking in the same direction , recalled him to himself he said returned the other said Mr Haredale , sitting down Feigning to be wholly unconscious of the abrupt wave of the hand which rendered this farewell tantamount to a dismissal , Mr Chester retorted with a bland and heartfelt benediction , and inquired of Gabriel in what direction HE was going replied the locksmith , hesitating said Mr Haredale , without looking towards them said Mr Chester with inconceivable politeness
