# text = They stood looking at each other , and at her retreating figure , and for a long time neither of them spoke said Mr Haredale at length rejoined the other , resuming his accustomed manner with infinite readiness , and throwing himself upon the bench with a weary air Mr Haredale surveyed him with a look of cold contempt he said , folding his arms returned his friend , as he lazily crossed his legs returned the other said Mr Chester with a languid smile Mr Chester kissed his hand gracefully ; and with the same tranquil face he had preserved throughout -- even when he had seen his companion so tortured and transported by his passion that his whole frame was shaken -- lay in his lounging posture on the seat and watched him as he walked away he said , raising his head to look after him The spot where they had met , was in an avenue of trees .
