# text = The old-fashioned furniture of the chamber , which was a kind of hospital for all the invalided movables in the house , grew indistinct and shadowy in its many shapes ; chairs and tables , which by day were as honest cripples as need be , assumed a doubtful and mysterious character ; and one old leprous screen of faded India leather and gold binding , which had kept out many a cold breath of air in days of yore and shut in many a jolly face , frowned on him with a spectral aspect , and stood at full height in its allotted corner , like some gaunt ghost who waited to be questioned .
