# text = But the difference between them lay in this : that whereas Mr Willet's extreme sagacity and acuteness were the efforts of unassisted nature , the Lion stood indebted , in no small amount , to beer ; of which he swigged such copious draughts , that most of his faculties were utterly drowned and washed away , except the one great faculty of sleep , which he retained in surprising perfection .
