# text = Mr Haredale entered first , and led the way through it into the latter chamber , where he seated himself at a writing-table from which he had risen when they had rung the bell he said , beckoning to old John , who remained bowing at the door he added hastily to Hugh , who entered also returned John , elevating his eyebrows , and lowering his voice to the tone in which the question had been asked him said Mr Haredale , looking towards him as he spoke returned Mr Willet , glancing over his shoulder at the organ in question said Mr Haredale Hugh shrugged his shoulders , and with a disdainful look , which showed , either that he had overheard , or that he guessed the purport of their whispering , did as he was told .
