# text = He'd drink the Thames up , if it was strong enough , sir , replied John Willet said Hugh As John made no reply , Mr Haredale brought out a glass of liquor , and gave it to Hugh , who , as he took it in his hand , threw part of it upon the floor said John Hugh rejoined , holding the glass above his head , and fixing his eyes on Mr Haredale's face With that he muttered something to himself , and drank the rest , and setting down the glass , preceded them without another word .
