# text = In less than an hour's time , supper had been served , and ate , and cleared away ; and Lord George and his secretary , with slippered feet , and legs stretched out before the fire , sat over some hot mulled wine together said Gashford , filling his glass with great complacency said his lordship , raising his head and here the secretary clasped his hands said Lord George said his lord said Lord George , thrusting his hands into his pockets , taking them out again to bite his nails , and looking uncomfortably at the fire said the secretary returned his lord he added , without waiting for an answer said the secretary , looking sharply at the other's downcast eyes , which brightened slowly as he spoke he cried with sparkling eyes cried the secretary , looking upwards he asked with evident delight he rejoined , moving uneasily in his seat , and biting his nails as though he would pare them to the quick whined Gashford , drawing his chair nearer with an injured air , and laying his broad flat hand upon the table he repeated , bending the dark hollows of his eyes upon him with an unwholesome smile replied the other , shaking him by the hand , rising from his seat , and pacing restlessly about the room he added as he made a sudden halt returned the pliant secretary repeated Gashford repeated Gashford again -- taking the lion's share of the mulled wine between whiles said Lord George with a heightened colour and in a louder voice , as he laid his fevered hand upon his shoulder , ' and are the only men who regard the mass of people out of doors , or are regarded by them , we will uphold them to the last ; and will raise a cry against these un-English Papists which shall re-echo through the country , and roll with a noise like thunder .
