# text = Not at all discomposed by the discovery , John Grueby fixed his hat on , wrongside foremost that he might be unconscious of the shadow of the obnoxious cockade , and withdrew to bed ; shaking his head in a very gloomy and prophetic manner until he reached his chamber Gashford , with a smiling face , but still with looks of profound deference and humility , betook himself towards his master's room , smoothing his hair down as he went , and humming a psalm tune .
