# text = Just as he has come upon the reader , he had come , from time to time , upon the public , and been forgotten in a day ; as suddenly as he appears in these pages , after a blank of five long years , did he and his proceedings begin to force themselves , about this period , upon the notice of thousands of people , who had mingled in active life during the whole interval , and who , without being deaf or blind to passing events , had scarcely ever thought of him before said Gashford in his ear , as he drew the curtains of his bed betimes returned the secretary , with meekly folded hands said Lord George , rubbing his eyes and looking round the room cried Gashford , with a smile returned his superior exclaimed the pious secretary , recoiling returned the other , very quickly the secretary cried , with looks of great surprise he muttered the secretary began he echoed , interrupting him returned the Secretary said Gashford , taking up Lord George's watch which lay upon a chair , and seeming to read the inscription on the seal , abstractedly .
