# text = He remained smiling in silence for a short time longer , and then said , slowly and distinctly returned the other , shaking his head said the secretary in the same mild tone , and with the same emphasis said Dennis , with another oath resumed Gashford , affecting not to hear the interruption said the fellow , with an ugly wink pursued the secretary , still smiling , and still managing his eyes so that he could watch him closely , and really not be seen in turn the hangman was beginning in a reckless way , when Gashford started forward , laid his finger on his lips , and feigned to write , just as the door was opened by John Grueby said John , looking in cried Gashford in his blandest voice But John had brought this new visitor to the door , and he walked in unbidden , as the words were uttered ; giving to view the form and features , rough attire , and reckless air , of Hugh The secretary put his hand before his eyes to shade them from the glare of the lamp , and for some moments looked at Hugh with a frowning brow , as if he remembered to have seen him lately , but could not call to mind where , or on what occasion .
