# text = Considering himself silently appealed to by this action , Mr Dennis shook his head thrice , as if to say of Gashford and hiding his profile from Hugh with one long end of his frowzy neckerchief , nodded and chuckled behind this screen in extreme approval of the secretary's proceedings asked Hugh said Gashford , opening his eyes to their utmost width wheezed the hangman under his breath Whether Hugh heard him , or saw by his manner that he was being played upon , or perceived the secretary's drift of himself , he came in his blunt way to the point at once he said , stretching out his hand and taking it back glancing at Dennis said Dennis approvingly cried Hugh rejoined the hangman With these and other expressions of confidence of the like flattering kind , Mr Dennis gave him a hearty slap on the back , which Hugh was not slow to return cried the hangman responded Hugh said the secretary with his usual mildness cried Dennis
