# text = Mr Tappertit sat and contemplated him for a long time in silence , as if he suspended his judgment ; then drew a little nearer to him , and eyed him over more carefully ; then went close up to him , and took him apart into a dark corner he began , with a thoughtful brow said Hugh , in his careless way returned Sim The encouraging way in which Mr Tappertit made this request , and coupled it with an assurance that he needn't be frightened , amused Hugh mightily -- so much indeed , that be saw nothing at all of the small man before him , through closing his eyes in a fit of hearty laughter , which shook his great broad sides until they ached again said Mr Tappertit , growing a little impatient under this disrespectful treatment cried Hugh Hugh opened his eyes on hearing this , and looked at him in great surprise said Mr Tappertit , pushing him away with a condescending playfulness Hugh faltered said Mr Tappertit Certainly Hugh did , and he remembered D . Varden too ; but that he didn't tell him said Mr Tappertit cried Hugh said Mr Tappertit cried Hugh said Mr Tappertit roared Hugh said Mr Tappertit With these conciliatory expressions he suited the action to the word ; and Hugh meeting his advances readily , they performed the ceremony with a show of great heartiness said Mr Tappertit , looking round on the assembled guests replied Hugh said Mr Tappertit , rubbing his palm upon his legs , and looking at it between whiles Hugh laughed again , and with such thorough abandonment to his mad humour , that his limbs seemed dislocated , and his whole frame in danger of tumbling to pieces ; but Mr Tappertit , so far from receiving this extreme merriment with any irritation , was pleased to regard it with the utmost favour , and even to join in it , so far as one of his gravity and station could , with any regard to that decency and decorum which men in high places are expected to maintain .
