# text = Nor was Hugh by any means a passive follower , who scrupled to act without precise and definite orders ; for when Mr Tappertit mounted on an empty cask which stood by way of rostrum in the room , and volunteered a speech upon the alarming crisis then at hand , he placed himself beside the orator , and though he grinned from ear to ear at every word he said , threw out such expressive hints to scoffers in the management of his cudgel , that those who were at first the most disposed to interrupt , became remarkably attentive , and were the loudest in their approbation .
