# text = These persons whispered very much among themselves , and kept aloof , and often looked round , as jealous of their speech being overheard ; some two or three among them entered in books what seemed to be reports from the others ; when they were not thus employed ) one of them would turn to the newspapers which were strewn upon the table , and from the St James's Chronicle , the Herald , Chronicle , or Public Advertiser , would read to the rest in a low voice some passage having reference to the topic in which they were all so deeply interested .
