# text = Miss Miggs went on to say that she would recommend all those whose hearts were hardened to hear Lord George themselves , whom she commended first , in respect of his steady Protestantism , then of his oratory , then of his eyes , then of his nose , then of his legs , and lastly of his figure generally , which she looked upon as fit for any statue , prince , or angel , to which sentiment Mrs Varden fully subscribed .
