# text = Mr Haredale is too just , too generous , too clear-sighted in his moral vision , to he rejoined with a sarcastic smile , finding the secretary stopped Gashford meekly shrugged his shoulders , and looking on the ground again , was silent interposed Sir John at this juncture said Mr Haredale replied Sir John , with an engaging smile said Gashford , fumbling with his gloves retorted Mr Haredale , with a bitter glance at the third party in their conversation said Sir John , in his most benignant way said Mr Haredale , declining the proffer with a motion of his hand replied Sir John sweetly Gashford , who had been very restless all this time , but had not once looked up , now turned to Sir John , and ventured to mutter something to the effect that he must go , or my lord would perhaps be waiting said Mr Haredale which he was about to do without ceremony , when he was stayed by a buzz and murmur at the upper end of the hall , and , looking in that direction , saw Lord George Gordon coming in , with a crowd of people round him .
