# text = But the throng of people -- the foremost of whom had heard every word that Lord George Gordon said , and among all of whom the rumour had been rapidly dispersed that the stranger was a Papist who was bearding him for his advocacy of the popular cause -- came pouring out pell-mell , and , forcing the nobleman , his secretary , and Sir John Chester on before them , so that they appeared to be at their head , crowded to the top of the stairs where Mr Haredale waited until the boat was ready , and there stood still , leaving him on a little clear space by himself .
