# text = Dennis placed a chair , his only one , for the secretary , in front of the hearth ; and took his seat again upon the stool he had left when he rose to give the visitor admission he said , as he resumed his pipe , and looked at him askew rejoined the secretary , with a friendly nod to Hugh growled the hangman cried Hugh said the secretary , with his worst expression of face , and in his mildest tones replied Hugh vociferated Dennis said the secretary , in as pastor-like a voice as if he were commending them for some uncommon act of valour and generosity and here he stopped and warmed his hands : then suddenly looked up Mr Dennis coughed and shook his head , as who should say Hugh sat and smoked in silence said the secretary , warming his hands again said Dennis , after looking at his face to assure himself that he was serious replied the secretary said the hangman , in his hoarest chuckle , as he pointed with his pipe to Hugh he added in a whisper , as he drew his stool close to him and jogged him with his elbow cried Hugh in a surly voice , as he overheard this last remark retorted Dennis , shaking his head , with a kind of pity for his friend's ingenuous youth said Gashford , smoothly grinned the hangman , whispering the words behind his hand .
