# text = Indeed , the bird himself appeared to know his value well ; for though he was perfectly free and unrestrained in the presence of Barnaby and his mother , he maintained in public an amazing gravity , and never stooped to any other gratuitous performances than biting the ankles of vagabond boys ( an exercise in which he much delighted ), killing a fowl or two occasionally , and swallowing the dinners of various neighbouring dogs , of whom the boldest held him in great awe and dread .
