# text = Pausing now and then to let his smoke curl slowly off , and to sniff the grateful fragrance of the flowers , he sat there at his ease -- as though the cottage were his proper dwelling , and he had held undisputed possession of it all his life -- waiting for the widow's answer and for Barnaby's return When Barnaby returned with the bread , the sight of the pious old pilgrim smoking his pipe and making himself so thoroughly at home , appeared to surprise even him ; the more so , as that worthy person , instead of putting up the loaf in his wallet as a scarce and precious article , tossed it carelessly on the table , and producing his bottle , bade him sit down and drink he said The water stood in Barnaby's eyes as he coughed from the strength of the draught , and answered in the affirmative said the blind man cried Barnaby returned the blind man with a sigh said Barnaby , drawing his chair nearer to him , and looking eagerly in his face he returned
