# text = The blind man passed his hand lightly over the poor fellow's face , and finding that his elbows were planted on the table , that his chin rested on his two hands , that he leaned eagerly forward , and that his whole manner expressed the utmost interest and anxiety , paused for a minute as though he desired the widow to observe this fully , and then made answer cried Barnaby , rubbing his hands said the blind man cried Barnaby , turning to her with delight said the blind man he slowly added she answered said Stagg , arising from the table She led him out at the door , and into the little garden , where they stopped she said , in a half breathless manner Stagg retorted she said returned the blind man calmly , after a long pause he added hastily
