# text = She told him in a timid manner ,-- for he was very loud , hoarse , and red-faced ,-- and besought him not to be angry , for they meant no harm , and would go upon their way that moment replied the gentleman cried the raven , whom Barnaby had shut up on the approach of this stern personage said the gentleman Barnaby , thus condescendingly addressed , produced his bird , but not without much fear and trembling , and set him down upon the ground ; which he had no sooner done than Grip drew fifty corks at least , and then began to dance ; at the same time eyeing the gentleman with surprising insolence of manner , and screwing his head so much on one side that he appeared desirous of screwing it off upon the spot .
