# text = Barnaby shook his head and looked vacantly from one to the other said Gashford the widow interposed said Lord George to his secretary cried Gashford with a solemn face said the widow said Gashford implored the widow , laying both her hands upon his breast , and scarcely knowing what she did , or said , in the earnestness of her supplication said Lord George , evading her touch , and colouring deeply said Gashford , with a kind of meek severity said Lord George , glancing at Barnaby , and whispering in his secretary's ear and here he turned red again replied the secretary he added , with a lip that slightly curled as he looked at Barnaby , who stood twirling his hat , and stealthily beckoning them to come away said Lord George , addressing him said Barnaby , with sparkling eyes replied Lord George , with a reproachful glance at the unhappy mother Barnaby kissed his mother tenderly on the cheek , and bidding her be of good cheer , for their fortunes were both made now , did as he was desired .
