# text = Among them were Simon Tappertit and Mr Dennis ; both of whom , but especially the latter , greeted Barnaby with the utmost warmth , and paid him many compliments on the prowess he had shown said Dennis , with an oath , as he rested his bludgeon in a corner with his hat upon it , and took his seat at the same table with them asked Mr Tappertit , who had been quenching his fiery face in a half-gallon can rejoined the hangman said the hangman , in a tone of deep disgust returned Simon Tappertit , going out in a lofty manner rejoined the hangman , calling after him meaning Hugh and Barnaby With which mournful review of their proceedings , Mr Dennis sought consolation in cold boiled beef and beer ; but without at all relaxing the grim and dissatisfied expression of his face , the gloom of which was rather deepened than dissipated by their grateful influence .
