# text = An honest confidence in the government under whose protection they had lived for many years , and a well-founded reliance on the good feeling and right thinking of the great mass of the community , with whom , notwithstanding their religious differences , they were every day in habits of confidential , affectionate , and friendly intercourse , reassured them , even under the excesses that had been committed ; and convinced them that they who were Protestants in anything but the name , were no more to be considered as abettors of these disgraceful occurrences , than they themselves were chargeable with the uses of the block , the rack , the gibbet , and the stake in cruel Mary's reign .
