# text = One fellow who wore the popular colour , damned them for not having cockades in their hats , and bade them set a good watch to-morrow night upon their prison doors , for the locks would have a straining ; another asked if they were fire-proof , that they walked abroad without the distinguishing mark of all good and true men ;-- and a third who rode on horseback , and was quite alone , ordered them to throw each man a shilling , in his hat , towards the support of the rioters .
