# text = Lord George , biting his nails in a discomfited manner , regarded Barnaby for some time in silence ; then beckoning to his servant , said John Grueby touched his hat , and came his master asked in a low voice said John Lord George demanded , faltering said John , with emphatic brevity said his master , speaking in a peevish tone John Grueby answered returned his angry master , glancing at himself returned the unmoved John cried his master , turning sharply upon him answered John said Lord George replied John , touching his hat respectfully said Lord George returned Lord George , motioning him to go back returned John Grueby cried Lord George , addressing Barnaby , who had looked on and wondered while this dialogue passed said John , in explanation cried Barnaby , putting the raven on the ground , and shouldering his staff said Lord George Bamaby's heart swelled within his bosom as he heard these words .
