# text = They were not long in reaching the barracks , for the officer who commanded the party was desirous to avoid rousing the people by the display of military force in the streets , and was humanely anxious to give as little opportunity as possible for any attempt at rescue ; knowing that it must lead to bloodshed and loss of life , and that if the civil authorities by whom he was accompanied , empowered him to order his men to fire , many innocent persons would probably fall , whom curiosity or idleness had attracted to the spot .
