# text = Mr Dennis , having by this time succeeded in extricating from his hat a great mass of pasty , which had been wedged in so tightly that it was not easily got out , put it before him ; and Hugh , having borrowed a notched and jagged knife from one of the company , fell to work upon it vigorously said Dennis , after a pause Hugh looked at him , and at the blackened faces by which he was surrounded , and , stopping for a moment to flourish his knife above his head , answered with a roar of laughter said Simon Tappertit retorted his lieutenant , parting the men who stood between them , with his knife , that he might see him said Simon retorted Hugh But as the majority of those present were by no means anxious for a second engagement that night , being already weary and exhausted , they sided with Mr Tappertit , and pressed him to make haste with his supper , for they had already delayed too long .
