# text = The carriage stopped again said Hugh to the man who opened the door , as he took Miss Haredale's hand , and felt how heavily it fell growled Dennis -- it was that amiable gentleman asked Hugh said the hangman Having by this time hoisted the young lady into his arms , he staggered off with his burden said Hugh , drawing Dolly towards him Thrusting his face away with all her force , and holding down her head , Dolly submitted to be carried out of the chaise , and borne after Miss Haredale into a miserable cottage , where Hugh , after hugging her to his breast , set her gently down upon the floor .
