# text = The room-door was closed and fastened to keep intruders at a distance , and then they proceeded to exchange news said Hugh Several cried that they did ; but the majority of the company having been engaged in the assault upon the Warren , and all present having been concerned in one or other of the night's expeditions , it proved that they knew no more than Hugh himself ; having been merely warned by each other , or by the scout , and knowing nothing of their own knowledge said Hugh , looking round him They shook their heads , and murmured an answer in the negative , as each man looked round and appealed to his fellow ; when a noise was heard without , and a man was heard to say that he wanted Hugh -- that he must see Hugh cried Hugh to those who kept the door muttered the others
