# text = Leaving the sexton at the horse's bridle , he drew out the chaise with his own hands , and would have harnessed the horses , but that the post-boy of the village -- a soft-hearted , good-for-nothing , vagabond kind of fellow -- was moved by his earnestness and passion , and , throwing down a pitchfork with which he was armed , swore that the rioters might cut him into mincemeat if they liked , but he would not stand by and see an honest gentleman who had done no wrong , reduced to such extremity , without doing what he could to help him .
