# text = With the intense impatience and excitement natural to one in his condition , Mr Haredale thrust himself forward and was about to speak , when the fat old gentleman interposed said he returned Mr Haredale , shaking his head said the old gentleman , calling up the stairs , to where the skirt of a dressing-gown fluttered on the landing-place replied a testy voice cried the old gentleman in a choleric manner said the Lord Mayor returned the old gentleman said the Lord Mayor returned the choleric old gentleman said the Lord Mayor whimpered the old gentleman , as he wiped his forehead in a state of ludicrous distress said the Lord Mayor , most emphatically returned the old gentleman said the Lord Mayor cried Mr Haredale , pressing the door open as the porter strove to shut it , and speaking rapidly cried the Lord Mayor said Mr Haredale cried the chief magistrate said Mr Haredale .
