# text = The cracks in the pavement of his cell , the chinks in the wall where stone was joined to stone , the bars in the window , the iron ring upon the floor ,-- such things as these , subsiding strangely into one another , and awakening an indescribable kind of interest and amusement , engrossed his whole mind ; and although at the bottom of his every thought there was an uneasy sense of guilt , and dread of death , he felt no more than that vague consciousness of it , which a sleeper has of pain .
