# text = Although the heat was so intense that the paint on the houses over against the prison , parched and crackled up , and swelling into boils , as it were from excess of torture , broke and crumbled away ; although the glass fell from the window-sashes , and the lead and iron on the roofs blistered the incautious hand that touched them , and the sparrows in the eaves took wing , and rendered giddy by the smoke , fell fluttering down upon the blazing pile ; still the fire was tended unceasingly by busy hands , and round it , men were going always .
