# text = When the sun rose , it shone into handsome apartments filled with armed men ; the furniture hastily heaped away in corners , and made of little or no account , in the terror of the time -- on arms glittering in city chambers , among desks and stools , and dusty books -- into little smoky churchyards in odd lanes and by - ways , with soldiers lying down among the tombs , or lounging under the shade of the one old tree , and their pile of muskets sparkling in the light -- on solitary sentries pacing up and down in courtyards , silent now , but yesterday resounding with the din and hum of business -- everywhere on guard-rooms , garrisons , and threatening preparations .
