# text = Sometimes , after every two or three mouthfuls , he laid down his knife and fork , and stared at his son with all his might -- particularly at his maimed side ; then , he looked slowly round the table until he caught some person's eye , when he shook his head with great solemnity , patted his shoulder , winked , or as one may say -- for winking was a very slow process with him -- went to sleep with one eye for a minute or two ; and so , with another solemn shaking of his head , took up his knife and fork again , and went on eating .
